.TH GECKO 1 "October 2026" "gecko" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gecko \- terminal multiplexer for coding agents across your machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gecko
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gecko keeps shells, tmux sessions, SSH connections and coding agents
running in a daemon and shows them in a web UI and a native window
(\fBgecko-desktop\fR(1)), on your desktop or your phone. Sessions survive
closing the window.
.PP
Without a command, \fBgecko\fR starts the daemon if needed, sets up start
at login the first time (undo with \fBgecko service uninstall\fR) and opens
the app.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open \fR|\fB url
Open the app, or print its URL with the access token.
.TP
.B ls \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List sessions on all hosts.
.TP
.B new \fR[\fIflags\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIcmd\fR]
Create a session.
.TP
.B attach \fIsession\fR
Attach this terminal (detach with Ctrl\-\e).
.TP
.B send \fIsession text\fR
Type text into a session.
.TP
.B capture \fIsession\fR
Print a session's text.
.TP
.B kill \fIsession\fR
End a session.
.TP
.B daemon \fR[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIaddr\fR]
Run the daemon in the foreground.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the daemon (ends all local sessions).
.TP
.B service install\fR|\fBuninstall
Start the daemon at login, or stop doing so.
.TP
.B help
All commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gecko-terminal
Configuration, settings, access token and state; \fBGECKO_HOME\fR moves it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gecko-desktop (1),
https://github.com/eternaleclipse/gecko
